codex
The nine goal-based tests pass, but a boundary review found one subtle Python datetime trap: two datetimes sharing the same `ZoneInfo` object can compare by wall clock across a DST fold, which can misclassify “before delivery.” I’m hardening the instant comparison through UTC and adding an ambiguous-hour regression test; I’m also correcting the timezone-conversion fixture so it uniquely exercises differing UTC and customer calendar dates.
apply patch
